# Sonic Frontiers (PPSA03831) -- title screen to gameplay (Cyber Space stage w6d01).
#
# Anchors are DISPLAY FLIPS ('f'), not seconds: the guest's own presented-frame counter is
# boot-speed invariant, and this title runs ~30 flips/s on a CPU-only boot_trace arm against
# ~3 flips/s on a live 3840x2160 renderer arm, so a wall-clock route cannot serve both.
#
# Route shape, and why each step exists (every claim below is measured, see
# docs/SONIC_FRONTIERS_STATUS.md):
#
# RUN THIS AGAINST AN EMPTY SAVE ROOT.
#
#     mkdir -p ~/prosper-run
#     PROSPER_SAVE0=$(mktemp -d -p ~/prosper-run) PROSPER_PAD_SCRIPT=@<this file> ...
#
# A FRESH directory each run, under $HOME rather than /tmp -- save_paths.hpp records that the save
# defaults were deliberately moved off tmpfs. Do not spell it with $$: that is the SHELL's pid, so two
# runs from one terminal share a directory and the second inherits the first's save, which is exactly
# the failure described below.
#
# MEASURED (2026-08-27, three arms of this route on one build): with `savedata0/PPSA03831/` present
# the run sits in the EXTRAS menu for its whole length -- 24/24 frames with content,
# `pixel-distinct=24`, guest healthy -- and never reaches the stage. With that directory moved
# aside, and again with PROSPER_SAVE0 pointed at an empty root, it reaches GameModeStage. So
# "save present => this route fails" is established.
#
# THE MECHANISM IS NOT. The plausible story is that the twelve confirms below assume the
# twelve-page queue a FIRST boot shows, so a shorter queue lets the surplus confirms fall through
# and activate the entry under the cursor ("Extras"). Nobody has counted the notice pages with a
# save present, and docs/SONIC_FRONTIERS_STATUS.md already records the SAME end state arising from
# flip/wall-clock desync under host load instead. Check `uptime` before blaming a save (#2790).
#
# Budget: single-run rates of 1.5, 2.8 and 3.4 flips/s were seen across three arms of this route,
# so f2900 (GameModeStage) landed between ~14 and ~32 minutes and one arm missed it inside a 1400 s
# timeout. `--render-every 6` moves the rate ~1.5x (2.84 -> 4.27) -- real, but not enough to make
# iteration cheap.
#
#   f1100-f1540   Twelve confirms, 40 flips apart, clear the twelve-page boot notice queue
#                 ("Extras", "Update notification", "Game update", "Update Details", "Update",
#                 "Additional options", "Action Marks", "New Game+", ...). The queue advances one
#                 page per FACE-button press; the d-pad does NOT advance it, so directional entries
#                 here would silently do nothing. The queue is modal over the title screen and is
#                 what a no-input arm sits behind forever.
#   f1700-f1940   Five 'up'. With the queue cleared the main-menu cursor rests on "Extras", the
#                 last of six entries (New Game, Language, Carry over from PlayStation(R)4,
#                 Copyright, User manual, Extras), so five 'up' land on "New Game" whether or not
#                 the list wraps. 60 flips apart: a single 4-flip press moves exactly one entry,
#                 while a long hold auto-repeats and lands somewhere else.
#   f2100         Confirm "New Game" -> a confirmation dialog opens.
#   f2300         Answer the dialog.
#   f2600         -> GameModeOpening: raw/ui/ui_gamemodeopening*.pac and raw/event/scene/ev0020*.
#   f2900         Skip into the stage -> GameModeStage: raw/ui/ui_gamemodestage*.pac,
#                 raw/stage/w6d01/w6d01_trr_s*.pac terrain sectors, raw/gedit/w6d01_gedit*.pac.
#   f3100+        Spare confirms for any further prompt, then left-stick input so the capture shows
#                 a moving player rather than a paused first frame.
#
# The main-menu entry list does not render its text on this build (#2206), so the cursor is moved
# blind and counted; the cursor bar itself does render and was used to verify the five moves.
#
# Fresh-save arms and inherited-save arms are NOT the same route: pass an isolated
# PROSPER_SAVE0=<private dir> so the notice queue is the measured twelve pages.

# --- boot notice queue: twelve confirms -------------------------------------------------------
f1100-1103:cross
f1140-1143:cross
f1180-1183:cross
f1220-1223:cross
f1260-1263:cross
f1300-1303:cross
f1340-1343:cross
f1380-1383:cross
f1420-1423:cross
f1460-1463:cross
f1500-1503:cross
f1540-1543:cross

# --- main menu: "Extras" -> "New Game" --------------------------------------------------------
f1700-1703:up
f1760-1763:up
f1820-1823:up
f1880-1883:up
f1940-1943:up

# --- New Game, its confirmation dialog, the opening, then the stage ---------------------------
f2100-2103:cross
f2300-2303:cross
f2600-2603:cross
f2900-2903:cross
f3100-3103:cross
f3300-3400:cross
f3600-3700:cross
f3900-4000:cross
f4200-4300:cross
f4500-4600:cross
f4800-4900:cross

# --- in the stage: hold forward, with a jump every so often, so any capture window lands on a
# moving player rather than a paused first frame. The blocks continue far past the point where
# control is handed over because the flip at which the post-cutscene load completes depends on
# how fast the host streams the stage, not on the route.

